# Radio ID aliases for the listening page (bin/mcfrs-ui). Copy to
# /etc/mcfrs-scanner/radio-ids.tsv on the box; the page reloads it when it changes.
#
#   <radio id><TAB><alias>            exact
#   re:<regex><TAB><template>         pattern, \1 \2 = groups (Python re syntax)
#
# There is no public alias list for this system any more (RadioReference removed
# theirs by policy, 2026 check), so this file is LEARNED FROM THE AIR: the page shows
# unknown IDs raw; when a unit identifies itself by voice ("Engine 714 driver"),
# write the ID down here. MCFRS radios live in the 2500xxx-2502xxx range
# (docs/SYSTEM.md). Examples below are placeholders, not real assignments.
# Confirmed on air 2026-09-03: small IDs (61, 67 seen) are the ECC dispatch consoles
# (RadioReference lists 66/67 as Fire/Rescue Dispatch).
re:^(\d{1,3})$	ECC console \1
#2501234	A714 Driver
#2501235	E714 Officer
#re:^25019(\d\d)$	Battalion Chief \1
